in{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(1,0),(0,1),(-2,1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e809067-fccf-511c-9fa9-c259ab9e7737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275894} {:answer/id #uuid "40ecaffa-3314-5656-b789-5511c190e435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276045} {:answer/id #uuid "483e2208-febd-5425-9f85-aeb182abec07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276118} {:answer/id #uuid "7a6406ee-ca13-59f3-9ded-4abe2538501a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276589} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c8ca19-6194-528b-b32e-041a39580876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e809067-fccf-511c-9fa9-c259ab9e7737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275894} :answer-field/id #uuid "59df823e-787f-5891-af52-12920962dd0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "932ec8a6-f54a-5a6e-82db-611776aadb8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-160644" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(2,-3),(3,1),(-4,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(3,2)$\n- $(1,-3)$\n- $(-1,4)$" :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{270}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-2),(1,-3),(-1,4).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f0666e-f729-5d5d-985b-9b3b5b14541c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275682} {:answer/id #uuid "630a936b-d542-585d-b79f-690989f4f5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276374} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ff9584-6905-5910-ae2e-3